                        "relativePublishTimeDescription":  "4 months ago",
                        "rating":  2,
                        "text":  {
                                     "text":  "For a pricey NT$4,000 omakase, the meal was a total letdown with dishes served in utter disarray: cold starters, then hot appetisers, followed by sashimi and then steamed egg. The jarring shifts in temperature and flavors felt chaotic and off-putting, nowhere near the seamless experience a proper omakase should deliver.\n\nThe atmosphere was downright stressful, the boss lady yelling, interrupting diners to chat, and barking at her staff right in front of everyone. She even scolded us for “eating and drinking too slowly,” making the whole evening tense and uncomfortable from start to finish.\n\nTo top it off, I ended up with gastroenteritis the next day. I wouldn’t recommend this restaurant.",
                                     "languageCode":  "en"
                                 },
